  "caption": "ONS estimates 246,000 British nationals left the UK long-term in the year ending December 2025, slightly fewer than the 257,000 estimated for the previous year. ONS says British emigration has been broadly stable in recent years, and the 2025 estimate is provisional.\n\nThese figures count long-term moves. They do not identify individual motives or prove that tax caused the departures.\n\nWhat evidence would you verify before making a relocation decision?\n\nSource: ONS: UK emigration explained, 21 May 2026.\nhttps://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/internationalmigration/articles/ukemigrationexplainedwhatweknowaboutbritsmovingabroad/2026-05-21\n\nPhoto: Finikoudes, Larnaca, Cyprus, Georgy Papantoniou, CC BY 3.0 (cropped).\nhttps://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finikoudes_by_Georgy_-_panoramio.jpg\nhttps://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\n\n#Cyprus #Relocation #UnitedKingdom #Migration #TheSmartySolution",
